================================================================================
ARCHITECTURAL SPECIFICATION (Locked)
================================================================================

AsyncTaskRouter Structure:
  - queue_tx: mpsc::Sender<MandateTask>
  - queue_size_limit: usize (default 10,000)
  - worker_count: u32 (default 8, 4x CPU cores in production)
  - circuit_breaker_state: Arc<Mutex<CircuitBreakerState>>
  - connection_pool_limit: Arc<Semaphore> (5 permits)
  - active_tasks: Arc<AtomicU32> (concurrency tracking)
  - max_concurrent_tasks: Arc<Mutex<u32>> (peak monitoring)

Execution Flow:
  1. submit_task(MandateTask) → try_send() to bounded channel
     - If queue full: Immediate CapacityExhausted (backpressure)
     - If success: Task queued, returns Ok(())
  
  2. Worker loop (8 concurrent workers):
     - recv() from channel (blocks until task available)
     - Acquire semaphore permit (blocks if 5 permits exhausted)
     - Increment active_tasks counter
     - Execute task (1ms simulated work)
     - Update max_concurrent_tasks if new peak
     - Decrement active_tasks counter
     - Release semaphore permit
     - Loop until channel closes

Backpressure Chain:
  1. Queue reaches capacity (10k tasks)
  2. Next submission → try_send() fails
  3. Caller receives CapacityExhausted
  4. Caller implements HTTP 429 (Too Many Requests)
  5. Circuit breaker can trigger if DB pool exhausted

